Chapter five: The domain of the undead

Galanda walked down the stairs, and the first thing she saw was a blue
bulging mass. Galanda instantly bashed it with her mace, but to her
surprise she felt a painful chill go through her body. Galanda paused
for a moment, then decided to leave it. This plan was shattered when
Ellora began to bite and slash the mass. Galanda could see Ellora
shiver in cold, and watched in horror as Ellora began to freeze to
death.

"Ellora! Stop!" yelled Galanda, quickly focussing her mind to heal the
damage. Ellora was on the brink of completely freezing, when she
stopped attacking and darted around. Galanda sighed in relief and
healed Ellora again. However once Ellora was healed she began to
attack the blue mould again. Galanda realised that Ellora was only
going to attacked when it was safe, so she looked around, fighting off
a few gnomes that were getting near, and found a scroll, which she
recognised as one of teleportation. Galanda walked back to Ellora, and
saw she was still playing with the mould. Galanda waited a while,
fighting off any monsters that would walk near. Soon the blue mould
had been killed and Galanda healed Ellora.

Galanda began to explore more of this level of caverns, keeping a
close eye on Ellora, and found another scroll of teleportation.
Galanda had explored most of the level when she saw a monkey come up.
Galanda was surprised that there would be any monkeys in a dungeon.
She was still wondering about this when the monkey jumped up and
grabbed her two scrolls of teleportation and started running away
screeching in laughing. Galanda angrily drew her mace and began to
chase the monkey, when she saw Ellora tripping near her and falling
down a large hole. Galanda paused for a moment and jumped down the
hole.

Galanda landed painfully on the floor and looked around. This level
was much brighter than the previous and she could see far away. In the
distance she could see Ellora fighting a few gnomes. Galanda quickly
walked over, picking up a scroll she found on the way. Ellora saw
Galanda and yipped, finishing off the nearby gnomes. Galanda smiled
and began looking for the stairs back up when the floor gave way
again, and she found herself falling through air again.

"Ellora!" yelled Galanda, but it was too late, and Ellora didn't hear
where Galanda had gone. Galanda fell for longer than before, and she
came to crash landing on top of a fountain. Galanda sipped from the
fountain, and was surprised when a nymph came out. Galanda barely had
time to draw her weapon before the nymph stole her blessed potion of
healing. Galanda angrily looked around but saw that the nymph had
disappeared. Galanda walked out of the small cavity she was in, and
found a long passage. At the end of that passage were two new long
passages. After a few more of these Galanda realised she was in some
kind of maze! Galanda sat on the floor wondering if she would be able
to get out.

Galanda suddenly heard a long crackling breath behind her. She looked
around and jumped up, since behind her was a vampire! Galanda dashed
down the passageway only to find a large zombie! However Galanda did
not become a priest without learning about this incarnations of the
dead. She quickly took out her garlic, and held it one hand, putting
her mace away. Galanda stood her ground as the vampire approached, and
began hitting the vampire with her garlic. To her satisfaction the
vampire screeched and fled, bumping into the walls in confusion and
stun. Galanda quickly switched for her mace, and approached the
zombie. Galanda recognised it's hideous form as one which used to
belong to an ettin. Galanda readied herself and ran into head forward
battle. Galanda struck several times with her mace before the ettin
reacted, striking her with a bandage covered fist. Galanda reeled in
pain, focussing her magic to numb and heal her pain. Galanda panic as
she realised it was becoming harder to focus her mind on spells.
Galanda began to assault the zombie again, hatred for the undead
begins fuelling her strength. Though Galanda was struck several more
times, the zombie soon fell.

Before Galanda even had a chance to rest, she heard the vampire come
from behind again. She grabbed her garlic, again stunning the vampire
to buy her time. Galanda fled down the passage, making a mental map of
where she was going. After a few minutes Galanda realised that there
was a large section where there seemed to be no entrance to. Either
her mapping was not as good as it used to be, or there was some hidden
way to enter. Galanda began searching the area, and sure enough found
a secret door. Looking though Galanda saw a large open area, with a
few minor zombies and a floating eye. Galanda sent the souls of the
dead onto the afterlife, and began to look around the room, carefully
avoiding the floating eye. Galanda found another scroll of genocide, a
blessed scroll of identify, a food ration and two spell books.

Galanda dispatched of the floating eye using her earlier tactic of
throwing her weapon at it, taking it from behind, then throwing it
again. Galanda locked the door in, had a quick snack of a slime mould,
and sat down to study the books. The first book she read contained the
knowledge of how to magically cause creatures to sleep. When Galanda
read the second book she suddenly felt a wrenching sensation, and was
sitting in an unfamiliar corridor, next to a vampire. Galanda grabbed
her garlic, shoving it at the vampire. The vampire screeched in pain,
and Galanda began attacking it while it was trying to flee. Once the
vampire was destroyed, she looked at the book again. This time she
could understand the runes, and learnt how to restore herself to her
former condition. Galanda was happy with these spells, and began
searching for the way back to the centre room.

Galanda was in the middle of a corridor when she heard a seducing
voice that sounded familiar. Behind her was the nymph that had her
equipment! Galanda drew her mace and attacked the nymph, but before
she could injure it, it stole her whistle and her shield! Galanda
angrily continued searching. She finally found the way back, and on
the way she found another spell book, and grey stone, and two
different scrolls she didn't know. Galanda again locked the door, and
read the new spell book. Inside it's covers was the knowledge of how
to induce fear into the hearts of enemies, Galanda threw the book away
in disgust. She did not need such an evil spell as that.

Galanda opened her backpack, and placed in all her items and her
weapon. She was about to close it when she heard a "scritch scritch"
sound from the grey stone rubbing against her mace. Peculiar...
thought Galanda. She decided to investigate further, so she took out
one of her scroll of identify, and used it to identify the stone. The
grey stone turned out to be a touchstone, used for identifying gems.
Galanda rubbed it against one of the gems she had picked up along her
journey. To her disappointment nothing happened. Galanda was not going
to just give up, and so dipped the stone into one of her remaining
potions of holy water. She again tried to use the touchstone and found
that it worked! Unfortunately the gem was only a piece of worthless
glass. Galanda took out her large masses of gems. She identified all
of them, and discovered she has a diamond and two emeralds! She
quickly threw away the rest of her useless gems, lightening her load
considerably.

Galanda walked back up the stairs, and did not recognise the level
above. It seemed she had fallen down more than one level. The level
was dark so she lit her lamp again. Unfortunately she could see the
lamp had little oil left. Galanda searched the level, and found not
one, but two new lamps! She also found a spell book, and attained a
wand of striking from a gnome king that tried to zap her with it.
Galanda read the spell book and learned the spell to illuminate dark
areas. Galanda continued up to the next level.

Again Galanda could not recognise the dungeon level she was now on.
The level was lit up and mostly open, so she took no time finding the
staircases. On the way she exchanged her rusty helmet for a new one,
and grabbed an elvish mithral chain mail, hoping it would fetch a high
price back in mine town. She also found a new rare gem, a chrysoberyl
stone!

As Galanda climbed the staircase to the next level she heard a
familiar barking in the distance. It was Ellora! Galanda looked
around, and saw Ellora fighting some more gnomes and another large
dog, and it didn't look too good for Ellora. Galanda blew her whistle
and ran up. Ellora saw her master and broke away from the enemies to
come to Ellora. Ellora grabbed her mace and began to fight the
enemies. Thankfully during the last two levels she had only had to
cast a spell once, and had regain almost full control over her magic,
therefore was able to heal herself while fighting. Ellora also came up
to help, but suddenly disappeared again!

Once the battle was over, Galanda found some kind of trap. She stepped
on it herself and was instantly teleported to a different section of
the caverns, near where she started. Galanda looked around and sure
enough saw Ellora again. Galanda ran over, but fell into a hidden pit,
filled with poisoned spikes. Galanda cried out in pain as the poison
seeped through hew body, greatly weakening her muscles. Galanda hauled
herself out with more difficulty than normal, and continued on, hoping
the poison would perhaps wear off. Too her dismay it didn't and she
sadly lead Ellora back up the stairs, taking a leash she found on the
way.

Soon Galanda reached mine town, and went straight to the shops to sell
her rare gems. She was given a large price for her diamond, but a much
smaller price for the chrysoberyl stone (still more than she had
gotten for Trollsbane though!). Unfortunately the general store
shopkeeper did not have enough money for the emeralds, and the other
shops wouldn't buy the gems. Galanda was still happy, because now she
had about $2500 in total! Galanda bought some candles in case she
needed them later, and an extra food ration, hauled Ellora away from
the guards, and continued back to the main dungeon. If she ever had to
enter those trap-filled mines again it would be to soon!

